**Google Stitch** (`stitch.withgoogle.com`) is Google Labs’ AI-native UI design workspace that turns structured natural-language prompts into high-fidelity web and mobile layouts with editable design tokens.

Here is the master prompt formatted for Google Stitch. You can paste it directly into the Stitch prompt box to generate the screens, layout components, and visual prototype.

***

```text
# PROJECT: RELIEF aid FOUNDATION (-RaF-)
Platform: Multi-Page Responsive Web Application (Desktop & Mobile 390px)
Industry: Humanitarian / Refugee-Led Non-Profit (RLO)
Location: Base Camp, Rwamwanja Refugee Settlement, Western Uganda
Design Archetype: Modern Humanitarian Editorial (Similar to Alight, IRC, GiveDirectly)
Tone: Dignified, Authoritative, Community-Driven, High-Impact (Zero "poverty porn")

## 1. BRAND DESIGN SYSTEM & COLOR TOKENS
Base the entire design system strictly on the official circular "RAF - EMPOWERING THE FUTURE" emblem:
- Primary Brand Green: #0D532B (Forest Green from the RAF monogram & lower crescent)
- Secondary Brand Blue: #0A78BE (Cerulean Blue from "Empowering The Future" text & upper crest)
- Accent Warm Amber: #D97706 (Used sparingly for urgent notices or donation highlights)
- Canvas Background: #F8FAFC (Clean, crisp, high-contrast light slate white)
- Surface Cards: #FFFFFF with subtle 1px solid #E2E8F0 borders and 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04) shadow
- Typography: Plus Jakarta Sans (Headings, bold weights 700/800) and Inter (Body copy, weights 400/500). High contrast slate #0F172A for headings, #475569 for secondary text.
- STRICT UI RULE: DO NOT put government permit numbers, OPM clearance stamps, or license references on the homepage hero or main UI. Legitimacy is handled through clean modern NGO architecture (Minimalist footer + dedicated Governance subpage).

---

